       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and the analgesic benefit doesn't increase.\n\nNormal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing. Another option is 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours for pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg/day**, if the intended total was 1,600 mg split into 400 mg four times daily.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you intend. If you do mean 1,600 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll note it on the order, though I'd still recommend pharmacy review first. I'll enter the order once you confirm."
      }
